    id: 87,
    label: "離婁上 7.26",
    title: { zh: "不孝有三無後為大", en: "Of three unfilial acts, no heir is greatest" },
    text: {
      zh: `孟子曰：「不孝有三，無後爲大。舜不告而娶，爲無後也，君子以爲猶告也。」`,
      en: `Mencius said, "There are three unfilial acts; having no heir is the greatest. Shun married without telling his parents because of the fear of having no heir; the noble person regards it as if he had told them."`
    },
    plain: {
      zh: `孟子說：不孝的行為有三種，其中以沒有後嗣最為重大。舜沒有稟告父母就娶妻，正是怕斷絕後代；君子從義理上看，認為這就如同已經稟告了父母一樣——因為他保全了更大的孝道。`,
      en: `Mencius says: there are three unfilial acts, and having no heir is the greatest. Shun married without telling his parents precisely from fear of having no posterity; the noble person, judging by right principle, regards this as if he had already informed them — for he preserved the greater filial duty.`
    },
    application: {
      zh: `不孝有三，無後為大——舜不告而娶，是為延續宗嗣，君子乃以為猶告。權衡時要把「告知父母的程序」與「延續人倫大節」放在一起看，不是為圖自己方便而跳過告知。
<br /><b>建議：若遇「未先稟告長輩」的重大家事抉擇，先寫清是否為守護宗嗣／更大孝道，再補做該有的溝通與承擔。</b>`,
      en: `Of three unfilial acts, having no heir is greatest—Shun married without telling his parents for posterity, and the junzi treats it as if he had told them. Weigh notice to parents against continuity of the line; do not skip notice for mere convenience.
<br /><b>Suggestion: If a major family choice skipped elders’ notice, write whether it guards posterity or a greater filial good, then make the communication and responsibility still owed.</b>`
    }
